; C21  Winning 42 pp. 106-108 (W42-p106-d, W42-p107-a, W42-p108-b; Hand 31)
; Rule, in our words: a bidder on lead holding both the 6-5 and the 6-4, neither
; of them trump, may lead the 6-5. A void opponent may trump it in case the
; 6-4 is elsewhere; the partner learns the bidder holds the 6-4.
; Python gate (pour_bidder gate_c21): the same, on any lead.
; How this encoding differs: none. The book plays it as a crisis lead in one
; hand; the gate, and this file, make it a rule on every lead.
(policy c21-six-five-bait
  (initial play)
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule lead-the-six-five (in play) (next play) (select tile 6-5)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles (chair b))
        (out)
        (pattern
          (viewer b)
          (declarer b)
          (leader b)
          (next-actor b)
          (own-legal 6-5)
          (own-legal 6-4)
          (not (in 6-5 q*))
          (not (in 6-4 q*)))))))
